From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bas=20Magr=C3=A9?= <bas@opvolger.net>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:07:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] PCI: spacemit-k1: Look up the root port by device_type
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

k1_pcie_parse_port() took the first available child node as the root
port.  With an INTx "interrupt-controller" child node placed before
"pcie@0" in the device tree, that node is picked instead; it has no
"phys" property, so probing fails with:

  spacemit-k1-pcie ca800000.pcie: error -ENODEV: failed to parse root port

Pick the child node with device_type = "pci" instead.

Signed-off-by: Bas Magré <bas@opvolger.net>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-spacemit-k1.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-spacemit-k1.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-spacemit-k1.c
index 04241df8fd59..12e9cd2dbcc2 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-spacemit-k1.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-spacemit-k1.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/err.h>
 #include <linux/gfp.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/syscon.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/phy/phy.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
@@ -258,8 +259,13 @@ static int k1_pcie_parse_port(struct k1_pcie *k1)
 	struct device_node *root_port;
 	struct phy *phy;
 
-	/* We assume only one root port */
-	root_port = of_get_next_available_child(dev_of_node(dev), NULL);
+	/*
+	 * We assume only one root port.  Skip the INTx interrupt-controller
+	 * child node, it is not a port.
+	 */
+	for_each_available_child_of_node(dev_of_node(dev), root_port)
+		if (of_node_is_type(root_port, "pci"))
+			break;
 	if (!root_port)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
